2026-09-27T07:42:43.4484266Z Update Note
2026-09-27T07:42:43.4484460Z ===========
2026-09-27T07:42:43.4484739Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T07:42:43.4485018Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:43.4485103Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T07:42:43.4485312Z ================
2026-09-27T07:42:43.4485434Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:43.4485584Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T07:42:43.4485945Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T07:42:43.4486149Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:43.4486261Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T07:42:43.4486526Z ====================================
2026-09-27T07:42:43.4486687Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:43.4486827Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T07:42:43.4487240Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T07:42:43.4487585Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T07:42:43.4488233Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T07:42:43.4488772Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:43.4488877Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T07:42:43.4489309Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T07:42:43.4489831Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T07:42:43.4490098Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:43.4490399Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T07:42:43.4490787Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:43.4490876Z Packages
2026-09-27T07:42:43.4491062Z ========
2026-09-27T07:42:43.4491167Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:43.4492435Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T07:42:43.4493744Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:43.4494317Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T07:42:43.4495745Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T07:42:43.4496959Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T07:42:43.4497976Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T07:42:43.4498919Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T07:42:43.4574334Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T07:42:43.4575280Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:43.4575470Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T07:42:43.4575879Z ==========================
2026-09-27T07:42:43.4576134Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:43.4577943Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T07:42:43.4579484Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:43.4580158Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T07:42:43.4581029Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T07:42:43.4581241Z 
